    "body": "## Problem\n\nDescribe the problem (concisely).\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nRelated: https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty/issues/8351#issuecomment-5113564951\n```\nkitty --config NONE -- nvim -u NONE +'map <s-space> <cmd>echo \"shift+space\"<cr>' +'map <space> <cmd>echo \"space\"<cr>'\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\nMaybe enable and handle \"Report associated text\".\nnvim can distinguish `<space>` and `<s-space>`\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-1201 g8b61626fb1` neovim/neovim@8b61626fb1\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.5-zen1-1-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n\n",
